flowchart TB
  accTitle: Ladybug architecture
  accDescr: One React PWA with a simulator mode, which runs both phones side by side with browser-local state and no account, and a connected mode installed on two phones. Connected writes queue offline, then go through Supabase RPCs, the only write path, into Postgres guarded by row-level security; photos are redrawn in the browser and stored privately. Realtime sends a hint back and Edge Functions deliver push notifications. Shared product rules keep the PWA and the earlier SwiftUI and Firebase app consistent. Self-hosted CI checks migrations, a three-account journey, and WebKit and Chromium runs.

  subgraph pwa["REACT PWA · ONE CODEBASE"]
    sim["`**Simulator mode**
    two phones, no account`"]
    app["`**Connected mode**
    installed on two phones`"]
    queue["`**Offline queue**
    IndexedDB`"]
  end

  subgraph supa["SUPABASE"]
    db[("`**Postgres**
    RLS + RPCs, Realtime`")]
    storage[("`**Private storage**
    redrawn JPEGs`")]
    fns["`**Edge Functions**
    push, support, places`"]
  end

  rules["`**Shared rules**
  shared/domain`"]
  ios["`**SwiftUI app**
  Firebase · earlier host`"]
  ci["`**Self-hosted CI**
  migrations, 3 accounts, e2e`"]

  app ==> queue
